  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Taxodone and FaDu, mediated through Leukocyte antigen CD37. Taxodone is reported to interact with CD37, which is a target of multiple compounds, including [(1S,2S,6R)-5,6-diacetyloxy-1-hydroxy-2-(2-hydroxyethoxy)cyclohex-3-en-1-yl]methyl benzoate, LTX-109, and Ficuseptamine B. All of these compounds are linked to FaDu, indicating a common downstream effect on the target cell. The scores for these relationships are consistent, suggesting a plausible biological pathway. The mechanism appears to involve CD37 as a central node, with Taxodone acting as a modulator of its activity. The evidence supports a possible role for Taxodone in influencing FaDu through CD37, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
